[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Clickwork
GenericName=Macro recorder
Comment=Record mouse and keyboard, replay it, or let a script watch the screen and decide
Comment[ru]=Запись мыши и клавиатуры, воспроизведение и скрипты, которые смотрят на экран
Exec=/usr/bin/clickwork
Icon=clickwork
Terminal=false
Categories=Utility;
Keywords=macro;recorder;automation;autoclicker;ocr;
StartupWMClass=io.github.blackixxce12.clickwork
# What KWin reads before it will hand this program its window protocol.
#
# KWin keeps five Wayland interfaces off the registry for ordinary clients and
# grants them only to a client whose executable resolves to a desktop file
# naming them here. Without this line a KDE session offers no window backend at
# all: no window steps, no anchoring, no workspace isolation, and nothing says
# why. `Exec` above must stay an absolute path, because that is what KWin
# matches against.
#
# The separator is a COMMA, not the semicolon a desktop file uses everywhere
# else. KWin reads the key through KService, which splits on KConfig's comma, so
# a semicolon-separated list arrives as one unrecognised string and the gate
# stays shut with no error anywhere. Measured both ways against KWin 6.7.5.
X-KDE-Wayland-Interfaces=org_kde_plasma_window_management,org_kde_kwin_fake_input
# A second gate, for a second thing, read the same way. KWin refuses
# `CaptureArea` to a client that is not named here, and since KWin implements no
# screencopy at all that refusal is the whole picture search, the text reader and
# the pixel condition at once.
X-KDE-DBUS-Restricted-Interfaces=org.kde.KWin.ScreenShot2
